 "text": "The closest thing to real mind control? A man in a lab coat. In 1961, Yale psychologist Stanley Milgram told volunteers to shock a stranger for every wrong answer. 15 volts, then 30, all the way to 450. He banged on the wall, then went silent. The man in the lab coat said, \"Please continue.\" Students predicted about 1% would go all the way. 65% did. The shocks were fake. The stranger was an actor. They didn't know. Here's the trick. Authority plus tiny steps. Each shock was just a little worse than the last. The antidote? When others refused, far fewer obeyed. So be the first to say no. Follow for more mind tricks.",
